[{:db/id 17592186133897 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-55130439-a2e5-560a-bbed-4ce47334253d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134386 :question/problem "![](images/01/01a5f06674cacca4764f438a8c06f020659f0177a0b74952f40bc9072627ec3f.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2},$ where \n\n- ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=2{t}^{2}\\,i-{t}^{3}\\,j$ for $t\\in [-1,1],$ and\n\n- ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(t)=2\\,i+t\\,j$ for $t\\in [-1,1].$\n\nUse Green's theorem to find the area of the region." :question/worked-solution "First, let $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$\n\nOur simple, piecewise-smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0-(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y=-{∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivatives of ${r}_{1}(t)$ and ${r}_{2}(t)$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\, & {r}_{1}^{′}(t)=4t\\,i-3{t}^{2}\\,j \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\, & {r}_{2}^{′}(t)=j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}}y\\,dx \\\\  & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}}y\\,dx-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}y\\,dx \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{t}^{3})\\cdot 4t\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}t\\cdot 0\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{4}\\,\\text{d}t-0 \\\\  & =4[\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186132355 :answer-field/correct 17592186132356 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133896 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-19d2b758-b269-5c92-aaaf-707449daf876" "question-30739161-7e72-5e37-b131-9975b77440f7" "question-6653118e-2998-5812-b728-f3217528d405"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-19d2b758-b269-5c92-aaaf-707449daf876" :question/id #uuid "19d2b758-b269-5c92-aaaf-707449daf876" :question/math-academy-id "q-42301" :question/problem "![](images/ac/ac9f6016ee4c93aec58f8fff0a8002057f89d7c1bae589e5357a25709ae5a76c.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩$ for $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{5\\pi }{3}].$ The area of $D$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}\\boxed{}\\,dt,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$ Determine the missing part of the equation." :question/worked-solution "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0-(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}-y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}-y\\,dx & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-53872032-3b68-54a9-b047-b5722ee1ce8d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-53872032-3b68-54a9-b047-b5722ee1ce8d" :answer-field/id #uuid "53872032-3b68-54a9-b047-b5722ee1ce8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-de993e24-618b-5743-81ef-393206c8a109" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b9f93b2c-abf4-5cbd-aa5b-d281bc9dc445" "answer-c3dbd51c-9d36-5509-bb8b-877222cbaef9" "answer-ba5cc6be-612b-5620-9ea1-537324d438b6" "answer-536ba388-fdb8-58ea-b126-38fbd2dcdb6b" "answer-de993e24-618b-5743-81ef-393206c8a109"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9f93b2c-abf4-5cbd-aa5b-d281bc9dc445" :answer/id #uuid "b9f93b2c-abf4-5cbd-aa5b-d281bc9dc445" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3dbd51c-9d36-5509-bb8b-877222cbaef9" :answer/id #uuid "c3dbd51c-9d36-5509-bb8b-877222cbaef9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba5cc6be-612b-5620-9ea1-537324d438b6" :answer/id #uuid "ba5cc6be-612b-5620-9ea1-537324d438b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-536ba388-fdb8-58ea-b126-38fbd2dcdb6b" :answer/id #uuid "536ba388-fdb8-58ea-b126-38fbd2dcdb6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de993e24-618b-5743-81ef-393206c8a109" :answer/id #uuid "de993e24-618b-5743-81ef-393206c8a109" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-30739161-7e72-5e37-b131-9975b77440f7" :question/id #uuid "30739161-7e72-5e37-b131-9975b77440f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-42315" :question/problem "![](images/bf/bfec7cbdb26a3db773ab1f6207de436ff0856b331cda183da530dbb6b91d91bd.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$r(t)=⟨{cos}^{3}⁡t,\\,{sin}^{3}⁡t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ].$ The area of $D$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\boxed{}\\,dt,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$ Determine the missing part of the equation." :question/worked-solution "Our simple, piecewise-smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0-(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}-y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-3{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}-y\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-{sin}^{3}⁡t)\\cdot (-3{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3{sin}^{4}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1007d99f-4a44-5eca-8672-e3953d3b25aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1007d99f-4a44-5eca-8672-e3953d3b25aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "1007d99f-4a44-5eca-8672-e3953d3b25aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-244e3377-d03b-59bc-9a15-821691749cc3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3b19e5e7-17b2-5ecd-8bda-2f5d049ec56f" "answer-01f00612-ca24-58a9-9a99-5bc9dff70695" "answer-4c93679f-96a9-5546-b831-28f2a59ed0bd" "answer-4ac2fdfe-d325-50d4-8f82-69274f9797ee" "answer-244e3377-d03b-59bc-9a15-821691749cc3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b19e5e7-17b2-5ecd-8bda-2f5d049ec56f" :answer/id #uuid "3b19e5e7-17b2-5ecd-8bda-2f5d049ec56f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{4}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01f00612-ca24-58a9-9a99-5bc9dff70695" :answer/id #uuid "01f00612-ca24-58a9-9a99-5bc9dff70695" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{sin}^{3}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c93679f-96a9-5546-b831-28f2a59ed0bd" :answer/id #uuid "4c93679f-96a9-5546-b831-28f2a59ed0bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{sin}^{3}⁡t{cos}^{3}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ac2fdfe-d325-50d4-8f82-69274f9797ee" :answer/id #uuid "4ac2fdfe-d325-50d4-8f82-69274f9797ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{sin}^{3}⁡t{cos}^{4}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-244e3377-d03b-59bc-9a15-821691749cc3" :answer/id #uuid "244e3377-d03b-59bc-9a15-821691749cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{sin}^{4}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6653118e-2998-5812-b728-f3217528d405" :question/id #uuid "6653118e-2998-5812-b728-f3217528d405" :question/math-academy-id "q-126746" :question/problem "![](images/0a/0a60729b626e1e9e219a839898cacc18aa81ec2a9b1b445e7b92b721874c2550.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ].$ The area of $D$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\boxed{}\\,dt,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x.$ Determine the missing part of the equation." :question/worked-solution "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }9{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f5a72b7a-4d2b-5cb1-bfa9-dcf075591732"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f5a72b7a-4d2b-5cb1-bfa9-dcf075591732" :answer-field/id #uuid "f5a72b7a-4d2b-5cb1-bfa9-dcf075591732" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6f80c7b4-33fd-57db-876b-025e20021ccd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81dd9c9a-88ed-5edc-bb4a-ab112606e4e5" "answer-e911610a-7c47-5303-9138-bd0e5e56ae76" "answer-bd4d50f5-796c-5fc2-a622-14130e42fc0e" "answer-6f80c7b4-33fd-57db-876b-025e20021ccd" "answer-14451dd1-51ba-5cb4-a62a-0a5d4ff055bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81dd9c9a-88ed-5edc-bb4a-ab112606e4e5" :answer/id #uuid "81dd9c9a-88ed-5edc-bb4a-ab112606e4e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e911610a-7c47-5303-9138-bd0e5e56ae76" :answer/id #uuid "e911610a-7c47-5303-9138-bd0e5e56ae76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9{sin}^{2}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd4d50f5-796c-5fc2-a622-14130e42fc0e" :answer/id #uuid "bd4d50f5-796c-5fc2-a622-14130e42fc0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f80c7b4-33fd-57db-876b-025e20021ccd" :answer/id #uuid "6f80c7b4-33fd-57db-876b-025e20021ccd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14451dd1-51ba-5cb4-a62a-0a5d4ff055bf" :answer/id #uuid "14451dd1-51ba-5cb4-a62a-0a5d4ff055bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{sin}^{2}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-55130439-a2e5-560a-bbed-4ce47334253d" :question/id #uuid "55130439-a2e5-560a-bbed-4ce47334253d" :question/math-academy-id "q-126757" :question/problem "![](images/ef/ef44f01fb462cdf608f66a60dd11b8df798603bd204dca9d579ed50b370a84e3.png)\n\nUse Green's theorem to find the area of the region enclosed by the curve \n$C$ parametrized as $r(t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\,j$ \nfor $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, let $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$\n\nOur simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is negatively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0-(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNotice that we have to take the line integral with a minus sign since our path is negatively oriented. \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate our line integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\text{d}u=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}y\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\cdot (-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡2t\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2{u}^{3}{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =2({1}^{3}-(-1)^{3}) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-589fe02c-92ec-567f-8354-84271d506420"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-589fe02c-92ec-567f-8354-84271d506420" :answer-field/id #uuid "589fe02c-92ec-567f-8354-84271d506420" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a6e358f5-54ad-55b9-afe1-8f1e0f017b3c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6e358f5-54ad-55b9-afe1-8f1e0f017b3c" "answer-6baabb12-e16e-5f6d-acae-67851198dc97" "answer-9beda9f3-8b47-5843-a2c9-b0565509b47e" "answer-30812918-b09d-5eac-98bf-46dd91f25063" "answer-079819d9-6be2-54b5-a40a-e93e9bbceca5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6e358f5-54ad-55b9-afe1-8f1e0f017b3c" :answer/id #uuid "a6e358f5-54ad-55b9-afe1-8f1e0f017b3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6baabb12-e16e-5f6d-acae-67851198dc97" :answer/id #uuid "6baabb12-e16e-5f6d-acae-67851198dc97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9beda9f3-8b47-5843-a2c9-b0565509b47e" :answer/id #uuid "9beda9f3-8b47-5843-a2c9-b0565509b47e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30812918-b09d-5eac-98bf-46dd91f25063" :answer/id #uuid "30812918-b09d-5eac-98bf-46dd91f25063" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-079819d9-6be2-54b5-a40a-e93e9bbceca5" :answer/id #uuid "079819d9-6be2-54b5-a40a-e93e9bbceca5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-5a146ad8-7f02-557a-a03b-2c457ab4ba04" :activity/id #uuid "5a146ad8-7f02-557a-a03b-2c457ab4ba04" :activity/title "Using Green's Theorem to Calculate Area" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050567 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-3efe2d38-47eb-5856-81a2-431378bd1194" "step-26451fe3-7951-51a8-9a1b-fd3d8660fd3b" "step-ad8a8662-52fd-53e4-8d4b-b923614bdc82" "step-db95ffdd-3589-5fdd-806c-5051d2294931" "step-7f777294-56ab-5734-acea-b53e1763dfff"] :activity/first-step "step-3efe2d38-47eb-5856-81a2-431378bd1194" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-3efe2d38-47eb-5856-81a2-431378bd1194" :step/id #uuid "3efe2d38-47eb-5856-81a2-431378bd1194" :step/content 17592186134386 :step/next "step-26451fe3-7951-51a8-9a1b-fd3d8660fd3b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-26451fe3-7951-51a8-9a1b-fd3d8660fd3b" :step/id #uuid "26451fe3-7951-51a8-9a1b-fd3d8660fd3b" :step/content "question-19d2b758-b269-5c92-aaaf-707449daf876" :step/next "step-ad8a8662-52fd-53e4-8d4b-b923614bdc82" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ad8a8662-52fd-53e4-8d4b-b923614bdc82" :step/id #uuid "ad8a8662-52fd-53e4-8d4b-b923614bdc82" :step/content "question-30739161-7e72-5e37-b131-9975b77440f7" :step/next "step-db95ffdd-3589-5fdd-806c-5051d2294931" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-db95ffdd-3589